  "T06_actual_entry": "| T06 | normal \u7cbe\u786e\u503c\u4e3a `(-1)^s (2^23+f)\u00b72^(E\u2212150)`\uff1bE=1..23 \u7684\u56e0\u5b50\u867d\u4e3a\u6b21\u6b63\u89c4\u6570\uff0c\u4e58\u79ef\u4e5f\u53ef\u7cbe\u786e\u6062\u590d normal | [R2-W03 \u62a5\u544a][W03]\u662f\u66f4\u5e7f\u6570\u5b66\u63a8\u5bfc\uff1b\u5f53\u524d\u5df2\u9a8c\u8f6c\u6362\u53ea\u5bf9 24..254 \u8d70\u5feb\u8def\uff0c\u5176\u4f59\u56de\u9000\uff1b\u4e0d\u80fd\u628a\u6269\u5927\u57df\u5f53\u6210\u5df2\u9a8c\u4f18\u5316 |",
  "mechanism_comparison": {
    "historical_math": "T06/R2-W03 already gives normal value sign*M*2^(E-150), including E1..23 with subnormal factor. R2-W03 section4 also describes two exact multiplications using normal factors to avoid a subnormal factor. Thus the general low-normal/two-scaling idea is not new.",
    "old_wide64": "Actual E102..151 path: UInt64 M shifted variably by E-102 or E-134, choose2^-48 or2^-16, UInt64.toFloat32, one multiply, withSign conditional. The signed variant uses Int64 sign construction. Neither is an implemented E1..23 rescaled-table path.",
    "new_unique_formula": "On original low guard rejection and magnitude>=0x00800000 only: tableProduct(u+0x10000000)*Float32.ofBits0x2f800000. This raises biased E1..23 to33..55, reuses the existing signed table and UInt32 mantissa conversion, then rescales by2^-32. No UInt64 shift, two-bucket selection or separate random sign branch. Two multiplications, existing table access and one closed constant remain.",
    "actual_new_contribution": "Conditional full-word proof using actual decoder/rounder/codec and no-wrap/sign/fraction preservation; targeted extension of the prior fallback domain. Distinct mechanism/placement does not establish speed.",
    "excluded": "E0 including subnormal/zero is not covered by standalone helper equivalence. Actual wrapper minnormal test excludes e0 in low false branch; +/-0 already pass the original wrapped low test and keep original table route. Inf/NaN and E24..254 retain original source mechanisms."
  },
